** ============================================================
** Horizontal Cantilever Beam — CalculiX CCX input file
** ============================================================
** Geometry  : 500 mm long × 20 mm wide × 10 mm tall
** Elements  : C3D8 (8-node linear hex), 25×2×1 mesh = 50 elements
** Units     : mm, N, MPa
** BCs       : Left face (x=0) fully fixed (U1=U2=U3=0)
** Load      : 100 N total downward (-Z) on right face (x=500)
**             distributed across 6 nodes (16.67 N each)
** Material  : placeholder — patched by prepare job
**
** Analytical solution (Euler-Bernoulli beam theory):
**   I = b h³/12 = 20×10³/12 = 1666.7 mm⁴
**   δ_tip = F L³ / 3EI
**   σ_max = F L (h/2) / I  at root (x=0)
**
**   Steel A36  (E=200000 MPa): δ=12.50 mm  σ=150.0 MPa  FoS=1.67
**   Al 6061    (E=68900  MPa): δ=36.28 mm  σ=150.0 MPa  FoS=1.84
**
**   FoS in orange zone (1.5-2.0) — makes report interesting.
**   Displacement differs 3× between materials — clearly visible.
**
** Note: set AppliedForceN=100 in values.yaml
** ============================================================

